      "status": "ok",
      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence directly states that Twitter makes better predictions about the inventory of languages used in each country (Abstract) and discusses the mechanism: in the Discussion, the authors note that Twitter has fewer missing languages (fewer false negatives) because Twitter data matches populations weighted by GDP better, implying it represents wealthier populations, and because the collection is based on urban areas. The Population Demographics section also notes Twitter better represents North America and Oceania. These constitute the authors' hypothesized/offered explanations for why Twitter captures more of the language inventory."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 2516.8200000189245
    },
